  (:adr/body
  "# ADR-2607184400: Bounded Kotoba HTTP response parsing and native read timeout

**Status**: accepted
**Date**: 2026-07-18

## Context

ADR-2607184300 established real HTTP/TLS component execution but accepted any
response beginning with a small fixed prefix. Also, Wasm instruction fuel
cannot interrupt a JVM HostFunction blocked inside a socket read.

## Decision

Keep protocol validation in `.kotoba`. The HTTP provider now parses and checks
the three-digit 100-599 status code and recursively scans, bounded by the
received buffer length and Wasm fuel, for the mandatory CRLF-CRLF header
terminator. Missing or malformed status/header framing returns minus one.

Add `:max-transport-read-ms` to RuntimeLimits and the canonical transport
contract. Native TCP and TLS sockets receive that finite SO_TIMEOUT before any
read or handshake. A real slow-peer test proves a blocked read returns minus
one within the configured boundary and leaves no live handle.

## Maturity boundary

Status and header framing are validated, but Content-Length reconciliation,
chunked decoding, multi-read assembly, redirect policy, header-name/value
limits and external interoperability remain pending. Redirects are not
followed implicitly, so they cannot expand endpoint authority today.
")))
